 R←Test_Misc_003(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;res
⍝ Runs the "LogForBranch" method against the fixture, whose history is known.
⍝ Note that "LogForBranch" reports what is unique to the given branch ("--not" all others), so
⍝ asking for "main" yields nothing at all: "feature" was branched off it and holds every one of
⍝ its commits. Asking for "feature" yields exactly the one commit made on it.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 res←∆Folder4 G.LogForBranch'feature'
 →T.PassesIf 2=⍴⍴res
 →T.PassesIf 4=2⊃⍴res                                  ⍝ Hash, committer, date and subject
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢res
 →T.PassesIf'Extra added on the feature branch'≡4⊃res[1;]

 →T.PassesIf 0=≢∆Folder4 G.LogForBranch'main'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
